@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Agent conversation startup ownership
+
+Concurrent starts on the same `AgentStrategy` previously created and selected separate conversations. Overlapping strategy instances could also publish an older conversation over a newer selection, and cleanup of one instance could clear another instance's selected pill conversation.
+
+Starts in the same instance and generation now share one creation promise, including its failure; a later call can retry after settlement. Cleanup advances the instance generation, so a new start does not wait for an old cancelled creation. The existing conditional creation removes a row that completes after cancellation. An older completion cannot clear a newer pending promise.
+
+New agent starts in this renderer carry a shared revision and a snapshot of the selected pill conversation. A pending creation is discarded if another agent start takes precedence or the selection changes. If that happens while the original instance is still current, startup rejects rather than silently recording with no conversation. Cleanup clears the pill selection only when it still names that instance's conversation.
+
+These checks are renderer-local and compare selection values, not a durable version: selecting another conversation and then returning to the original value before completion is not detected. Typed-message events share a separate renderer-local creation promise. They conditionally register only while no pill conversation is selected, so a concurrent agent or manual selection wins rather than being overwritten. Creation failures and superseded selection are reported to the user, but the original typed text is not restored automatically. Typed and agent creation are not one unified operation; whichever publishes first can cause the other to be discarded. An already-invoked conversation write cannot be cancelled; cleanup of a discarded row can fail and that failure propagates. The tests use mocked repositories and do not establish cross-process behavior.
