@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# API-key failure disclosure
+
+Provider integration tests and API-key repository operations can reject with arbitrary error text. That text may echo a submitted credential or provider response. The API-key settings test now shows a generic failure instead of the raw provider exception. API-key load, create, update, delete and update-reconciliation paths likewise log, display and propagate generic errors rather than forwarding the original exception. Load cancellation remains distinguishable from a normal load failure. The settings form consumes rejected save promises without logging their raw errors a second time.
+
+This is a deliberate diagnostics tradeoff: these paths no longer expose the native/provider failure detail. It is not a claim that every other provider, settings, preference, or network path sanitizes errors. The shared preference writer has separate safeguards described in `preference-failure-disclosure.md`; other preference paths may still report their own errors. Calls already made to providers and any copies held by those providers cannot be recalled. The tests inject mocked errors and do not establish native IPC or live-provider behavior.
