+# Azure streaming failure ownership
+
+An Azure recognition error after startup previously only logged the SDK cancellation and later returned accumulated text as a successful transcript. The stream now records that failure, closes its resources, stops accepting audio and rejects finalization rather than silently returning a partial transcript. A cancellation while finalization is waiting rejects that same shared finalization promise promptly; repeated calls share the outcome. SDK stop failures also reject instead of reporting partial success. Cancellation, stop and asynchronous startup errors use generic diagnostics so raw SDK details cannot leak through these paths.
+
+This does not guarantee complete transcription in all cases: the existing two-second stop timeout still returns the accumulated transcript when no explicit error arrives, and an error after a finalization has already resolved cannot retract it. Synchronous stream setup and start exceptions also become generic errors unless the caller has aborted. One-shot transcription and other Azure/provider paths have separate handling. The desktop base session turns a rejected finalize into a null transcript and warning; behavior beyond that boundary depends on the caller's recovery path. Tests use a mocked SDK and do not establish live Azure behavior.
