+The provider-mark consolidation adds vendored SVGs, a checked-in generated React module and generator, provider marks in model/key/disclosure settings, provider-name search aliases, a provider id alongside the existing audio-disclosure name, and a preview demo using the desktop FormatJS transform. It also narrows Gladia resampler allocations to ordinary `ArrayBuffer`s and updates the shared media-query test harness and sandbox guidance. The privacy sentence and local/remote decision remain driven by the existing disclosure logic; the mark is decorative, not a security indication. The merge applied cleanly after reconstructing the already-integrated `0dddebb6` ancestry following a workspace Git-metadata reset.
+
+The imported logo map now checks own properties so malformed persisted provider IDs such as `constructor` cannot be mistaken for known artwork. The artwork tests verify generation drift and attributes, contrast calculations and rendering with mocks/jsdom, not trademark rights or actual visual appearance on every platform. Multiple instances of one mark can still contain identical document-wide SVG ids; different providers are namespaced, while identical artwork currently uses identical definitions. The bundled artwork's third-party provenance and licensing are described in its README; no independent legal review is implied.
