+The style-hotkey dialog retains the guarded write queue and clear-data lease while passing its open-time snapshot to the native compare-and-swap; conflict recovery reloads the group. A cancelled-before-start typing outcome must not retire the protected backlog. Transcription refresh retains concurrent additions and orders session-only rows against the published records. The receiver retains the base's newline requirement and per-frame authorization, while aligning its inclusive frame limit with the existing channel's payload-only limit.
