@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Transcription list refresh ownership
+
+Home and History can refresh the shared transcription list concurrently. A snapshot taken before a newly recorded or received transcription was saved could replace the list after that transcription was inserted into the store, hiding it until another refresh. An older refresh could also overwrite a newer published refresh.
+
+Each refresh now records the visible IDs at the beginning of its repository read and retains locally added, still-present rows that arrived during that read, inserting them by creation time. The existing session-only merge also orders against freshly fetched rows rather than only the pre-refresh map. A later successfully published refresh prevents an earlier one from publishing; an unmounted or failed newer refresh does not suppress a still-active older refresh. Existing deletion-revision retries and privacy-clear generation checks remain in force.
+
+The guarantee is renderer-local and depends on creation paths inserting their IDs into the shared state. It does not serialize external database writers or resolve edits made outside the renderer. Rows already present before a read are intentionally not retained just because they are in memory: an authoritative list may have removed them. Equal timestamps retain insertion-dependent ordering, and repeated deletion changes can keep a refresh retrying. Repository reads are not cancellable; clear only prevents their results from being published.
+
+The Home activity aggregate loader also rejects a snapshot if a clear began or completed during its read, and does not start new activity reads while a clear is pending. The activity read itself is not cancelled, and an already visible aggregate is not independently zeroized by that loader; normal clear recovery and application reset still own clearing displayed state. If a clear is cancelled or fails, a later focus or activity event is needed to refresh its loading status.
+
+Both History and Home now also check the shared pending-clear marker while starting and completing reads. A marker that appears and disappears entirely between checks in a different renderer still cannot advance this renderer's generation.
+
+Pending transcription deletion now coalesces repeated resume attempts while native deletion is in flight and rejects attempts to re-arm undo after the delete has started. Scheduling also fails explicitly when the clear gate is closed, so the row UI does not claim that an unscheduled deletion can be undone. A failed resumed delete remains queued and can be retried after its prior attempt settles. This is an in-renderer guard, not a cross-process transactional delete, and a hung native delete keeps its lease and in-flight slot until it settles.
