index 00000000..7414ae80
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/updater-trust-anchor.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Updater trust-anchor consistency
+
+Date: 2026-11-08
+
+The release build injects `UPDATER_PUBLIC_KEY` into each platform's Tauri configuration, then the publish job verifies detached signatures using its own view of that secret. If the secret changes between jobs, signatures can verify against the publish-time key while one or more installers were configured with a different updater trust anchor.
+
+Each signed platform build now reads its post-build Tauri configuration, verifies that updater artifacts are enabled and that the configured public key matches that job's key, and uploads a platform-specific SHA-256 digest of the configured value. Before signature verification or publication, the publish job requires the evidence from macOS, Windows and Linux and compares each digest with the publish-time public key. Missing, malformed, linked or mismatched evidence fails closed. Only the digest is uploaded; the key itself is not printed or uploaded by this check.
+
+This is configuration evidence, not a cryptographic attestation of the bytes embedded in each installer. It assumes the build consumed the checked configuration and that its workflow and artifacts are trusted. A real signed multi-platform release is still needed to validate Tauri's effective configuration, artifact layout, signature verification and GitHub upload end to end. Key rotation also needs a migration plan for already-installed clients, whose embedded trust anchor does not change merely because the release secret changes.
