+# Vendored toolchain manifest mismatch
+
+On 2026-11-08, an Arena agent sandbox downloaded the `vendor/sandbox-toolchain` archive at commit `8442ae0c4e8d0c6a3e2a54072c53e8db5e0fa9e7` and followed its reassembly and checksum procedure. `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256` reported one mismatch, for `README.md`. All other listed files passed.
+
+The manifest expects SHA-256 `7a4b8e36abaf778d7685d65c142a8cc2548e863f2cdee9840e866a42343550fe`. The downloaded README has SHA-256 `45b0df5d322ce846377a832df74651a51a224f5cbba45c77ff8ea61e2766f5a7`. Its Git blob ID is `df5c6f0beebf84ba117436db3061b06f904c3bb5`, which matches the GitHub contents API for that commit. The mismatch is therefore present in the pinned branch contents, rather than evidence that this download changed the README.
+
+The fetch procedure requires every manifest entry to pass. On 2026-11-08, the user authorized an exception for this README mismatch after the other entries passed. A second download reproduced the same mismatch. Its manifest and README Git blob IDs matched the pinned commit's GitHub contents API, and the other 14,441 manifest entries passed. This permitted use of that payload for this review, but did not make the old manifest valid.
+
+The vendor branch was subsequently amended to commit `82b2f98368b5e7d3234ddf35cff2d4395ec75e07`. Comparing the recursive GitHub trees for both commits found 14,438 blobs in each and exactly two changed blobs: `README.md` and `MANIFEST.sha256`. Both new files were fetched and checked against their Git blob IDs. The manifests differ only in the README entry, and the new README's SHA-256 matches that entry (`32f2c462cd15e535f723eea968fdfe3851a8f8b9bf1e288ad1b5b58a8d4bccdf`). Replacing those two files in the already checked payload and rerunning `sha256sum -c` verified all 14,442 entries. The toolchain binaries and archives are unchanged between the two commit trees.
